# getdatasource Function Documentation Fixes

This file contains all the changes needed to fix syntax errors and enhance the getdatasource examples.
Apply these changes after making your commit.

## File 1: content/terraform-policy/v0.1.x (beta)/docs/policy/reference/functions/getdatasource.mdx

### Change 1: Fix AMI filter syntax and add enhancements (around line 125)

FIND:
```
### Retrieve an AMI by filter

In the following example, the `core::getdatasource` function retrieves an AWS AMI that matches the filter.

```hcl
locals {
  amazon_linux_ami = core::getdatasource("aws_ami", {
    most_recent = true
    owners      = ["amazon"]
    filter      = {
      name   = "name"
      values = ["amzn2-ami-hvm-*-x86_64-gp2"]
    }
  })
}

resource_policy "aws_instance" "approved_ami" {
  enforce {
    condition     = attrs.ami == local.amazon_linux_ami.id
    error_message = "Instance must use the latest approved Amazon Linux 2 AMI: ${local.amazon_linux_ami.id}"
  }
}
```
```

REPLACE WITH:
```
### Retrieve an AMI by filter

In the following example, the `core::getdatasource` function retrieves an AWS AMI that matches the filter and validates both the AMI ID and name pattern.

```hcl
locals {
  amazon_linux_ami = core::getdatasource("aws_ami", {
    most_recent = true
    owners      = ["amazon"]
    filter      = [
      {
        name   = "name"
        values = ["amzn2-ami-hvm-*-x86_64-gp2"]
      },
      {
        name   = "virtualization-type"
        values = ["hvm"]
      }
    ]
  })
  ami_name_valid = core::regex_match(local.amazon_linux_ami.name, "^amzn2-ami-hvm-.*-x86_64-gp2$")
}

resource_policy "aws_instance" "approved_ami" {
  enforce {
    condition     = attrs.ami == local.amazon_linux_ami.id
    error_message = "Instance must use the approved Amazon Linux 2 AMI: ${local.amazon_linux_ami.id}"
  }

  enforce {
    condition     = local.ami_name_valid
    error_message = "AMI name must match Amazon Linux 2 pattern. Found: ${local.amazon_linux_ami.name}"
  }
}
```
```

